// GoldenCensus — the goldens on disk that NOTHING COMPARES, named on every suite run.
//
// ⚖ **THE GOLDENS ARE REFERENCE, NOT A GATE** (user ruling 2026-08-02). This file REPORTS and judges
// nothing: it touches neither the failed count nor the exit code. What makes a run red is a spec test
// failing — a wrong exit code, wrong stdout, a diagnostic that did not match, a compile that should have
// succeeded, a leak.
//
// ⛔ **A GOLDEN WHOSE CASE NO LONGER EXISTS IS UNREACHABLE FROM EVERY OTHER DIRECTION.**
// `SpecTestRunner.checkTestFragment` opens `<fragmentDir>/<test.name>.test` BY PATH and never
// enumerates, so an orphan is structurally invisible to the comparison itself; and `git diff` and
// `git status` say nothing about it either, because the file is tracked and unchanged. ⇒ A golden whose
// case was RENAMED, split or deleted stays on disk and agrees with nothing — a reference that cannot be
// wrong because nothing reads it. This enumeration is the only thing that finds them, and `W136`'s
// review found 58 by hand before it existed.
//
// **It rides the suite because the suite is the one thing every rung runs**, exactly as
// `requireLadderIndexComplete` and `requireHarnessRefusalsFire` do for their tree-level properties. A
// `scripts/` gate would be a second thing to remember to run.
//
// ⛔ **THE PREDICATE IS THE SPEC'S OWN ROSTER AND THE LANE'S NAME — NEVER WHAT THIS RUN EXECUTED.** A
// `--filter` run executes a handful of cases; keyed on "did this case run", this would scream on every
// filtered run and would be switched off inside a week. Every term below is read out of the spec TEXT
// and out of the lane directory's own name, so a filtered run, a full run, a cross-target run and a run
// on another host all produce the identical answer.
//
// ⚠ **A GOLDEN PRESENT ON ONE LANE AND ABSENT ON ANOTHER IS NOT A FINDING, and lane symmetry is never
// asked.** Measured: `fragments/x64-linux/field-declared-unknown-type/…-nameable-at-a-parameter.test`
// exists on x64-linux and on no other lane, legitimately — a lane's goldens accrete as that lane is
// run. The question is only ever whether THIS lane can ever compare THIS file.
//
// ⚠ **IT COVERS EVERY LANE, not this run's target** — orphan debris accretes fastest on the lanes
// nobody runs, where neither a compare nor a mint ever visits the directory. Which is why a lane's
// Target comes from its DIRECTORY NAME rather than from the run.
//
// ⚠ **A DISABLED OR TARGET-GATED CASE PRODUCES NO GOLDEN, and that is not a debt.** This asks only
// whether what EXISTS can be compared; it has no model of what ought to exist.
//
// ⚠ A finding is NOT always "delete the file": a case may have been RENAMED, in which case the golden
// should be renamed with it, so **the count is also a lower bound on renames nobody noticed.**

// Where a spec directory's goldens live — and whether it has any at all. A spec directory that pins no
// codegen (every harness fixture sub-run, for one) owes this census nothing.
union GoldenRoot
	at(root FilePath)
	none
end 'GoldenRoot'

function goldenRootIn(specDir FilePath) returns GoldenRoot
	let root = specDir.join("{FragmentsSubdir}")
	if not Directory.exists(root) 'noGoldensAtAll'
		return GoldenRoot.none
	end 'noGoldensAtAll'

	return GoldenRoot.at(root)
end 'goldenRootIn'

// The case names of one spec — its roster, and the subset of it a given lane can pin. A set rather than
// a walk per file: a spec's goldens are checked against its roster once per file, and a linear scan
// there would make the census quadratic in a spec's case count (`vector.md` alone declares 118).
typealias SpecCaseNameSet = Set with String

// The spec NAMES the corpus declares — a different question from the one above, asked of the same
// spelling. Named separately because `collectGoldensOfVanishedSpecs` reads it as "is there a spec called
// this", and a parameter typed `SpecCaseNameSet` there would be describing the wrong membership.
typealias SpecNameSet = Set with String

// What a `fragments/<name>` directory turned out to be. A directory whose name resolves to no target
// this compiler builds for is a THIRD answer rather than a silent skip: it is the shape a renamed or
// retired target leaves behind, and everything under it is unreachable by every lane at once.
union GoldenLaneTarget
	builds(target Target)
	namesNoTarget
end 'GoldenLaneTarget'

// One `fragments/<name>` directory: where it is, what it is called, and what that name resolves to.
//
// The name is stored rather than derived, because it is the ONLY spelling available on the
// `namesNoTarget` arm — `targetToString` has nothing to say about a directory that names no target.
type GoldenLane
	export let dir as FilePath
	export let name as String
	export let target as GoldenLaneTarget

	export static function create(dir FilePath, name String, target GoldenLaneTarget) returns GoldenLane
		return Self{dir: dir, name: name, target: target}
	end 'create'
end 'GoldenLane'

typealias GoldenLaneArray = Array with GoldenLane

// ⭐ **THE CENSUS.** Called by the PARENT after the verdicts and the summary, on every run.
//
// `effectiveTarget` is this RUN's target and is used for ONE thing: `parseSpecFile` resolves the
// target-qualified ```Stdout: / ```Stderr: / ```Maxoncstderr: fences against it. Every field this
// census reads — a case's name, its `<!-- targets: -->` restriction, its trace directive, its section
// pins — is the same whichever key the parse was given, which is what lets ONE parse per spec answer
// for all four lanes.
export function reportUncomparedGoldens(specDir FilePath, effectiveTarget Target)
	match goldenRootIn(specDir) 'goldens'
		none then return
		at(fragmentsRoot) then reportUncomparedUnder(fragmentsRoot, specDir: specDir, effectiveTarget: effectiveTarget)
	end 'goldens'
end 'reportUncomparedGoldens'

// The census proper, once its root is known. Split from the guard above only because a `match` arm is
// one expression and this is the whole walk.
function reportUncomparedUnder(fragmentsRoot FilePath, specDir FilePath, effectiveTarget Target)
	var entries = StringArray.create()
	let lanes = goldenLanesIn(fragmentsRoot, entries: entries)

	// ⭐ SPEC-OUTER, LANE-INNER, so each spec is parsed ONCE and asked of every lane. The other nesting
	// reads more naturally and costs four parses of the whole corpus.
	var declaredSpecs = SpecNameSet.create()
	let specPaths = try specFilePaths(specDir) otherwise panic("GoldenCensus.reportUncomparedUnder: could not list the spec directory. The parent already listed it to build this run's plan (SpecWorkerPool.buildPlans), and a run that selected nothing never reaches here.")

	for specPath in specPaths 'eachSpec'
		let specName = specPath.stem()
		declaredSpecs.insert(specName)

		let specFile = try parseSpecFile(specPath, effectiveTargetKey: targetToString(effectiveTarget)) otherwise panic("GoldenCensus.reportUncomparedUnder: a spec the parent already parsed to build this run's plan no longer parses.")
		// Every ACTIVE case this spec declares. A `<!-- disabled-test: … -->` case is deliberately NOT one:
		// it is never compiled, never run and mints no golden (`SpecParser`'s header), so a `.test` bearing
		// its name is a file nothing compares — which is precisely this census's finding, and an enabled
		// case may never be re-disabled.
		let roster = caseNameSetOf(specFile.tests)

		for lane in lanes 'eachLane'
			collectUncomparedIn(lane, specName: specName, specFile: specFile, roster: roster, entries: entries)
		end 'eachLane'
	end 'eachSpec'

	collectGoldensOfVanishedSpecs(lanes, declaredSpecs: declaredSpecs, entries: entries)

	let headline = "note: {entries.count()} golden fragment(s) under {fragmentsRoot.toString()} {UncomparedHeadline}. GOLDENS ARE REFERENCE, NOT A GATE:\n{ResultNoteIndent}nothing failed on this and the exit code is unaffected. Each file below is a reference that cannot be wrong,\n{ResultNoteIndent}because no case on that lane ever reads it. DELETE it — or, if its case was RENAMED, rename the file with\n{ResultNoteIndent}it, which is the reading this count is also a lower bound on.\n"
	reportResultNote(entries, headline: headline)
end 'reportUncomparedUnder'

// Every `fragments/<name>` lane directory, with what its name resolves to. A stray FILE directly under
// `fragments/` is reported rather than skipped: the goldens live two levels down, so nothing there is
// compared by anything either.
function goldenLanesIn(fragmentsRoot FilePath, entries StringArray) returns GoldenLaneArray
	var lanes = GoldenLaneArray.create()

	let listed = try Directory.list(fragmentsRoot) otherwise 'cannotList'
		entries.push(uncheckedEntry("{fragmentsRoot.toString()} could not be listed, so NOTHING below it was censused"))
		return lanes
	end 'cannotList'

	for entry in listed 'eachEntry'
		let name = entry.filename()
		if not Directory.isDirectory(entry) 'notALane'
			entries.push(uncomparedEntry("{FragmentsSubdir}/{name}", reason: UncomparedReason.strayUnderFragmentsRoot))
			continue
		end 'notALane'

		// The lane's target comes from its own name, matched against the one table `--target` is matched
		// against (`Main.parseBuildTarget`) — a second reader of that spelling is how a report comes to
		// describe a lane the compiler cannot name back.
		let resolved = match parseBuildTarget(name) 'resolution'
			resolved(target) gives GoldenLaneTarget.builds(target)
			unrecognized gives GoldenLaneTarget.namesNoTarget
		end 'resolution'

		lanes.push(GoldenLane.create(entry, name: name, target: resolved))
	end 'eachEntry'

	return lanes
end 'goldenLanesIn'

// ⭐ **THE CASE NAMES OF A LIST OF CASES — the ONE loop that turns cases into a set.** Both sets this
// census compares are built from one: the spec's whole ROSTER and the subset one lane can SELECT. They
// were two identical four-line loops, and a rule about which cases count (a name normalization, say)
// landing on one of them would have made the two sets answer different questions while still being
// compared to each other.
function caseNameSetOf(tests SpecTestArray) returns SpecCaseNameSet
	var names = SpecCaseNameSet.create()
	for test in tests 'eachTest'
		names.insert(test.name)
	end 'eachTest'
	return names
end 'caseNameSetOf'

// The cases `lane` can ever compare a golden for — asked of `selectedTests`, the harness's ONE selection
// door, rather than of a second copy of its rules. `filter` is empty because a filter is a property of
// one command line and this is a property of the tree; `includeNetwork` is TRUE because a
// `<!-- network: live -->` case IS compared under `--network`, so its golden is not dead.
//
// A lane whose name resolves to no target can select nothing: no run of any command line visits it.
function pinnableOn(lane GoldenLane, specFile SpecFile, specName String) returns SpecCaseNameSet
	return match lane.target 'resolution'
		builds(target) gives selectableCaseNamesOn(target, specFile: specFile, specName: specName)
		namesNoTarget gives SpecCaseNameSet.create()
	end 'resolution'
end 'pinnableOn'

// The half of the answer that needs a real target — split out only because a `match` arm is one
// expression and this one is a loop.
function selectableCaseNamesOn(laneTarget Target, specFile SpecFile, specName String) returns SpecCaseNameSet
	let selection = selectedTests(specFile, specName: specName, filter: "", effectiveTarget: laneTarget, includeNetwork: true)
	return caseNameSetOf(selection.selected)
end 'selectableCaseNamesOn'

// One spec's goldens on one lane, when a spec of that name still exists. The DIRECTORY guard and the
// per-lane pinnable set are this arm's own; the walk itself is not — see `collectGoldensIn`.
function collectUncomparedIn(lane GoldenLane, specName String, specFile SpecFile, roster SpecCaseNameSet, entries StringArray)
	let specGoldens = lane.dir.join(specName)
	if not Directory.isDirectory(specGoldens) 'laneHasNoneForThisSpec'
		return
	end 'laneHasNoneForThisSpec'

	let pinnable = pinnableOn(lane, specFile: specFile, specName: specName)
	collectGoldensIn(lane, specName: specName, specGoldens: specGoldens, classify: UncomparedClassifier.againstRoster(pinnable, roster: roster), entries: entries)
end 'collectUncomparedIn'

// ⭐⭐ **THE ONE WALK OVER ONE SPEC DIRECTORY'S GOLDENS — and it is one walk because the difference
// between a live spec and a vanished one is a CLASSIFICATION, nothing else.**
//
// ⛔ It was two, and they were identical line for line: where to look, what counts as a golden, how an
// entry reads, and what to say when the directory will not list. The failure that shape invites is this
// census's own thesis pointed at itself — a new rule about which files it enumerates lands on the
// live-spec copy, goldens under a live spec go on being censused, goldens under a VANISHED spec quietly
// stop, and **absence is the one thing no gate in this tree can see.** The orphan gate catches a census
// that has stopped working; it cannot catch one that has stopped working in half the tree.
function collectGoldensIn(lane GoldenLane, specName String, specGoldens FilePath, classify UncomparedClassifier, entries StringArray)
	let listed = try Directory.list(specGoldens) otherwise 'cannotList'
		entries.push(uncheckedEntry("{specGoldens.toString()} could not be listed, so its goldens were not censused"))
		return
	end 'cannotList'

	for entry in listed 'eachEntry'
		if entry.fileExtension() != FragmentExtension 'notAGolden'
			continue
		end 'notAGolden'

		match goldenVerdictOf(entry.stem(), lane: lane, specName: specName, classify: classify) 'verdict'
			compared then continue
			uncompared(reason) then entries.push(uncomparedEntry("{lane.name}/{specName}/{entry.filename()}", reason: reason))
		end 'verdict'
	end 'eachEntry'
end 'collectGoldensIn'

// How the walk above decides what one golden is. The ONLY thing that differs between the two callers,
// which is why it is a parameter and not a second copy of the walk.
union UncomparedClassifier
	// A spec of this name exists: the file is fine when the lane can select its case, and otherwise
	// carries one of the two reasons `uncomparedReasonFor` tells apart.
	againstRoster(pinnable SpecCaseNameSet, roster SpecCaseNameSet)
	// No spec of this name exists, so nothing under here can be compared by anything and no per-file
	// question is worth asking.
	everyFileOfAVanishedSpec
end 'UncomparedClassifier'

// What one golden IS. A union rather than an optional reason, so "this file is fine" carries no
// vestigial text and there is no sentinel to re-derive.
union GoldenVerdict
	compared
	uncompared(reason UncomparedReason)
end 'GoldenVerdict'

function goldenVerdictOf(caseName String, lane GoldenLane, specName String, classify UncomparedClassifier) returns GoldenVerdict
	return match classify 'how'
		everyFileOfAVanishedSpec gives GoldenVerdict.uncompared(UncomparedReason.noSuchSpec(specName))
		againstRoster(pinnable, roster) gives rosterVerdictOf(caseName, lane: lane, specName: specName, pinnable: pinnable, roster: roster)
	end 'how'
end 'goldenVerdictOf'

// The half of the answer that needs the two sets — split out only because a `match` arm is one
// expression and this one is a guard plus a call.
function rosterVerdictOf(caseName String, lane GoldenLane, specName String, pinnable SpecCaseNameSet, roster SpecCaseNameSet) returns GoldenVerdict
	if pinnable.contains(caseName) 'thisLaneComparesIt'
		return GoldenVerdict.compared
	end 'thisLaneComparesIt'

	return GoldenVerdict.uncompared(uncomparedReasonFor(lane, caseName: caseName, specName: specName, roster: roster))
end 'rosterVerdictOf'

// WHY a lane does not pin a golden it holds — and the answers need different fixes, which is why they
// are not folded into one sentence. A case nobody declares wants the FILE changed; a case its lane
// cannot select wants the MARKER read, and may want it widened instead.
function uncomparedReasonFor(lane GoldenLane, caseName String, specName String, roster SpecCaseNameSet) returns UncomparedReason
	match lane.target 'resolution'
		namesNoTarget then return UncomparedReason.laneNamesNoTarget(lane.name)
		builds then break 'resolution'
	end 'resolution'

	if not roster.contains(caseName) 'noSuchCase'
		return UncomparedReason.noSuchCase(specName, caseName: caseName)
	end 'noSuchCase'

	return UncomparedReason.laneCannotSelectIt(specName, caseName: caseName, laneName: lane.name)
end 'uncomparedReasonFor'

// The goldens of a spec that is not there any more: a whole `.md` renamed or deleted leaves its entire
// per-spec directory behind on every lane at once. Swept after the per-spec pass because it is the
// complement of it — the directories no spec claimed.
function collectGoldensOfVanishedSpecs(lanes GoldenLaneArray, declaredSpecs SpecNameSet, entries StringArray)
	for lane in lanes 'eachLane'
		let listed = try Directory.list(lane.dir) otherwise 'cannotList'
			entries.push(uncheckedEntry("{lane.dir.toString()} could not be listed, so its spec directories were not censused"))
			continue
		end 'cannotList'

		for entry in listed 'eachEntry'
			let specName = entry.filename()
			if declaredSpecs.contains(specName) 'aSpecStillDeclaresIt'
				continue
			end 'aSpecStillDeclaresIt'

			if not Directory.isDirectory(entry) 'strayFile'
				entries.push(uncomparedEntry("{lane.name}/{specName}", reason: UncomparedReason.strayUnderLane))
				continue
			end 'strayFile'

			collectGoldensIn(lane, specName: specName, specGoldens: entry, classify: UncomparedClassifier.everyFileOfAVanishedSpec, entries: entries)
		end 'eachEntry'
	end 'eachLane'
end 'collectGoldensOfVanishedSpecs'

// ⭐ **ONE ENTRY OF THE CENSUS, AND THE ONE PLACE ITS TEXT IS SPELLED.** A path a reader can act on,
// then why nothing reads it, at `ResultNoteIndent` — the depth every other trailer in this suite puts a
// case at, because a reader takes the trailers as one column.
//
// EXPORTED, with `UncomparedReason` and `UncomparedHeadline`, because `HarnessSelfTest`'s orphan gate
// asserts on these exact lines. It builds its expectations by CALLING this, the way
// `requireNetworkGateHolds` builds its own from `verdictLine` and `resultNoteEntry`: a gate that spelled
// the sentence itself would be one fact written twice, and the half that drifts is always the one
// nothing renders.
export function uncomparedEntry(relPath String, reason UncomparedReason) returns String
	return "{ResultNoteIndent}{relPath} — {uncomparedReasonText(reason)}\n"
end 'uncomparedEntry'

// Every way a golden on disk can be one that nothing compares. A closed union rather than a String built
// at each site: the gate one level up asserts that three of these arms actually fire, and it can only do
// that against a set something enumerates.
export union UncomparedReason
	// The spec is there and active; it declares no case by that name. Rename debris, or a deletion.
	noSuchCase(specName String, caseName String)
	// The spec declares the case, but this lane can never select it — so its golden there is unreadable
	// reference whatever the compiler emits.
	laneCannotSelectIt(specName String, caseName String, laneName String)
	// No spec of that name exists at all: a whole `.md` renamed or deleted, leaving its directory behind.
	noSuchSpec(specName String)
	// A `fragments/<name>` directory naming no target this compiler builds for.
	laneNamesNoTarget(laneName String)
	// A file where only a lane directory belongs.
	strayUnderFragmentsRoot
	// A file where only a per-spec directory belongs.
	strayUnderLane
end 'UncomparedReason'

// The sentence each arm reads as. Split from the union so the arms carry the data and this carries the
// wording — and so a gate can name an arm without quoting a sentence.
function uncomparedReasonText(reason UncomparedReason) returns String
	return match reason 'reason'
		noSuchCase(specName, caseName) gives "{specName} declares no case named `{caseName}`"
		// Selection's remaining gates are all the spec's own text: a `<!-- targets: … -->` restriction, a
		// trace directive only x64-windows can capture, a section pin a container format cannot answer, or
		// a `status: draft` spec. Naming WHICH would mean re-deriving `selectableThisRun`'s conjunction
		// here, and a second copy of it is worth less than the sentence that sends the reader to the case.
		laneCannotSelectIt(specName, caseName, laneName) gives "{specName} declares `{caseName}`, but no run on {laneName} can select it — read its markers and its spec's status"
		noSuchSpec(specName) gives "no spec named `{specName}` exists, so nothing on any lane declares this case"
		laneNamesNoTarget(laneName) gives "`{laneName}` names no target this compiler builds for, so no run of any command line visits this lane"
		strayUnderFragmentsRoot gives "a file directly under the fragments root, where only per-target lane directories live"
		strayUnderLane gives "a file directly under a lane directory, where only per-spec directories live"
	end 'reason'
end 'uncomparedReasonText'

// The words the census's headline is recognised by — its one spelling, shared with the gate that
// asserts a tree with nothing to report prints NO such headline.
export let UncomparedHeadline = "are COMPARED BY NOTHING"

// A part of the tree the census could NOT read. Reported inside the same list rather than swallowed:
// "we chose not to look" must never read as "we looked".
function uncheckedEntry(what String) returns String
	return "{ResultNoteIndent}{what}\n"
end 'uncheckedEntry'
